From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qdsp6: scope prepare-time port start to MI2S

ROCKNIX carries the prepare-time start from its SM8750 tree for the Odin 3
AW88166 PLL-lock sequence, but Armada uses one kernel across SM8550, SM8650
and SM8750. Limit the workaround to playback MI2S backends so it does not
change prepare/trigger ordering for unrelated LPASS DAIs.

---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
@@ -233,7 +233,10 @@ static int q6apm_lpass_dai_prepare(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 	 * PCM trigger; start the port here so BCLK is up in time. The
 	 * trigger's !is_port_started guard then no-ops. Playback only.
 	 */
-	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK) {
+	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK &&
+	    ((dai->id >= PRIMARY_MI2S_RX && dai->id <= QUATERNARY_MI2S_TX) ||
+	     (dai->id >= QUINARY_MI2S_RX &&
+	      dai->id <= QUINARY_MI2S_TX))) {
 		rc = q6apm_graph_start(dai_data->graph[dai->id]);
 		if (rc < 0) {
 			dev_err(dai->dev, "Failed to start APM port %d\n", dai->id);
